solution.p:
The maximum value of the directional derivative at (-1, 1) is 
given by the magnitude of the gradient at (-1, 1): 
\; \left| \nabla f(-1, 1) \right| =  \sqrt{1669.14}

The minimum value of the directional derivative at (-1, 1) is 
given by 
-\left| \nabla f(-1, 1) \right| =  -\sqrt{1669.14}
